// A `match` no arm covers. Under the current typechecker this is
// actually caught statically ("non-exhaustive match"), not at runtime
// (see src/lib.rs's own comment on match_with_no_matching_arm_panics --
// a statically-exhaustive match can no longer fail at runtime with "no
// pattern matched"); kept as-is per Task 4's own instructions since the
// underlying feature (an arm set that doesn't cover its scrutinee) is
// genuinely impossible to reach at runtime through a typechecked
// program. Both binaries must still agree on the (typecheck) error.
match 5 | 1 -> 1
